    "gold_confidence": "high",
    "gold_justification": "The trial design is solid, but the investigator's statement 'already convinced' and\nextension to 'people of all ages' clearly exceeds what a 6-week study on 89 autistic\nadults can support. The overclaim is in the interpretation, not the methodology.\n",
    "gold_alternative_reading": "If one reads 'already convinced' as casual optimism rather than a scientific claim,\nthe case weakens. But the explicit generalization to 'all ages' from a narrow sample\nis a textbook unsupported generalization. The alternative reading is weak.\n",
    "gold_case_type": "clear",
    "curator_notes": "Good discriminative case: tests whether agents can separate study quality from claim\nquality. Both sprints show strong model agreement with the gold label (5/6 correct).\nThe one miss was Opus in Sprint 1 — too charitable with investigator rhetoric.\n"
